# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file every `docker build` and
# every `docker compose up` ships the whole repository as build context — 1,379
# tracked files, most of which the build never reads.
#
# vendor/ is NOT excluded, and must not be: the build is deliberately hermetic
# (`go build -mod=vendor` with no network), which is what lets a stranger build
# offline and what stops a release publishing an unbuildable binary.
# TWO Dockerfiles share this ONE context. deploy/docker/Dockerfile builds the
# app, and deploy/docker/docs.Dockerfile builds the docs image — and docs.yaml
# builds it with `context: .`, the repo root, so these patterns apply to it too.
# docs.Dockerfile:9 does `COPY docs-site/build /srv`, so excluding docs-site
# outright breaks every docs deployment with
# `failed to compute cache key: "/docs-site/build": not found`.
#
# Hence the re-include below. It MUST stay after the `docs-site` line: patterns
# apply in order, so a negation above the exclusion it reverses does nothing.
# docs-site/build is generated, not tracked — docs.yaml runs `npm run build`
# before the image build — so this re-includes an artifact that only exists in
# CI, and excludes the ~18 tracked sources that the app image never reads.
.git
docs
docs-site
!docs-site/build
*.md
